Operator asked if any recursive-refiner option ships pre-trained ARC weights. Weight-
availability workflow (5 models) + independent HF-API verification: YES.

#1 (USE) arcprize/trm_arc_prize_verification — the ARC Prize ORG's own TRM verification
checkpoints. HF-API VERIFIED: MIT, ships BOTH arc_v1_public/step_518071 AND
arc_v2_public/step_723914 + trm.py/losses.py/all_config.yaml; loads into local ~/trm_src.
Better provenance than re-training our untrained local TRM.
Fallbacks: Sanjin2024/TinyRecursiveModels-ARC-AGI-1/-2 (community, ~41% ARC-1 pass@2),
sapientinc/HRM-checkpoint-ARC-2 (official, ARC-2 only, HRM!=TRM arch).

Caveats: (1) transductive/per-puzzle-embedding -> needs TTA+augmentation+majority-vote
harness, not a plain forward (~11pp of score is that layer); (2) step_* are raw
torch.save pickles -> sandbox first load, re-serialize to safetensors.

Reframed next step (zero training): download #1 -> sandbox-load -> reproduce ARC baseline
-> HYBRID PROOF: rank TRM's candidate grids with the v2 grid verifier
(arc_grid_combined_verifier); does verifier-selection beat TRM's majority-vote on ARC-1/2?

